      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is a core financial provision established at issuance, making its applicability contingent on the policy being active since the issue date.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="e2e0db09-1411-4193-961b-49f641340784">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is a defining characteristic of the 20-Year Level Term Life Insurance policy, specifying its payout capacity.</data>
      <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="c3e2289f-6e9b-4f8f-8308-ced029f5f506">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is the key financial provision of the policy, determined at issuance regardless of ownership. It remains unchanged even though John Michael Anderson is designated as the policy owner.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="7f8cb083-f7ed-4837-a460-150e15a7c2d1">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $500,000 death benefit implies a specific financial obligation linked to the insured’s demise, reinforcing the significance of identifying the insured—John Michael Anderson—as central to the policy's purpose.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="46205e89-c698-46b2-991f-35e0dd9be668">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is a fixed contractual obligation that exists independently of the insured’s current age.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="9b6acf89-8e86-43c2-878b-9300e5dc9a2b">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit amount of $500,000 is independent of the insured’s date of birth, as it is determined by the policy terms rather than demographic details.</data>
      <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="70feef39-e3b5-4a93-9e69-79a091efe2e9">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit amount of $500,000 is fixed regardless of when the policy expires. This figure remains constant throughout the 20-year term until payout conditions are met.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="68115e7f-f7b6-423f-93fb-d3d8750f2e29">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is payable specifically to the designated primary beneficiary, Sarah Elizabeth Anderson, should the insured pass away during the policy term.</data>
      <data key="d4">PAYEE_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="24f6a5ad-25db-42dc-939d-c4d5b2ed9a0f">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is fully allocated to Sarah Elizabeth Anderson as the designated primary beneficiary, meaning she receives the entire sum upon the insured’s death.</data>
      <data key="d4">FULLY_ALLOTTED_TO</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="086e886c-9134-4e1e-85d7-0fcdb31e485b">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is intended for Sarah Elizabeth Anderson, whose status as the insured’s spouse explains her eligibility as the primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="61095de3-b57e-4b5b-ba01-9a506f62acd3">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit of $500,000 establishes the financial payout available under the policy, which would be distributed to contingent beneficiaries such as Lucas if the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="53ad6f3d-85c7-46d3-8a96-bb170408cdd8">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit of $500,000 establishes the financial payout available under the policy, which would be distributed to contingent beneficiaries such as Emma Grace Anderson if the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured.</data>
      <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="b0753f1c-4ff3-48b1-9b47-e666a0d807ea">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit of $500,000 is available to the primary beneficiary and contingent beneficiaries like Lucas if conditions are met. Lucas’s status as the son of the insured supports his eligibility as a contingent beneficiary under the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELEVANT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="7f9cc4e6-7309-41fc-89b5-a0f2bf367607">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit serves as the basis for calculating Lucas’s share, which is determined to be 50% based on equal distribution among contingent beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit of $500,000 specifies the payout upon the insured's passing, but it does not influence or relate to the monthly premium due date set for the 15th.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specifies the payout upon the insured's passing, independent of payment timing. The grace period allows continued coverage despite late payments, ensuring benefits remain available unless the policy lapses entirely.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="b573dc79-16fa-4d62-ac47-9944687f176c">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit amount of $500,000 is a fixed payout specified in the policy but unrelated to the timing of annual policy anniversaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the exact amount of the death benefit, which is only meaningful because fact_sentence_2 clarifies the definition of a death benefit as the payout made upon the insured's death during the policy term.</data>
      <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="c213cb6d-bc43-42c0-9cc8-b53860ab254b">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit specifies the sum payable to beneficiaries upon the insured's passing, independent of how premiums are paid. This information does not rely on nor influence details about premium collection frequency.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="92e1786a-d888-499c-81ce-89af6f2f700d">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the payout amount upon death, while fact sentence 2 specifies the recurring cost to maintain coverage. These details serve different purposes in the policy’s structure without influencing each other directly.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="b9bffd3e-9339-46c9-88e5-c86723b048a8">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit is only payable if the insured dies within the defined 20-year policy term, making the duration essential to the payout's validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9" target="a04dd995-de44-4f7d-adaa-d6a1e6223a7e">
      <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit establishes the total payout available, which is split evenly between contingent beneficiaries Emma and Lucas when the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured.</data>
      <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
