      <data key="d3">The definition of a grace period explains how late payments are handled, but it does not depend on or reference the policy’s issue date, making the reverse relationship non-informative.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="e2e0db09-1411-4193-961b-49f641340784">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period ensures that the terms of the 20-Year Level Term Life Insurance remain enforceable despite minor delays in premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="c3e2289f-6e9b-4f8f-8308-ced029f5f506">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage despite missed premium deadlines; since John Michael Anderson is the policy owner, he benefits from this provision when managing his monthly obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO_OWNER</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="7f8cb083-f7ed-4837-a460-150e15a7c2d1">
      <data key="d3">The grace period mechanism ensures continued coverage for John Michael Anderson even if he misses a premium deadline, reinforcing protection based on his role as the insured party.</data>
      <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO_INSURED</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="9b6acf89-8e86-43c2-878b-9300e5dc9a2b">
      <data key="d3">Understanding the grace period does not require knowledge of the insured’s date of birth; it pertains to payment timing rather than identity or demographics.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9">
      <data key="d3">The grace period maintains active coverage beyond the due date, preserving eligibility for the full death benefit should the insured pass during this time.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="46205e89-c698-46b2-991f-35e0dd9be668">
      <data key="d3">The concept of a grace period explains how coverage persists beyond the payment deadline, unrelated to the insured’s age, which only affects underwriting and premiums but not the timing mechanism of the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="b9bffd3e-9339-46c9-88e5-c86723b048a8">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a 31-day grace period depends on the policy having an established term—such as the 20-year term—which governs when payments are due and how long coverage may continue past missed deadlines.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="92e1786a-d888-499c-81ce-89af6f2f700d">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay the $45 monthly premium without losing coverage, providing flexibility around the payment deadline.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="c213cb6d-bc43-42c0-9cc8-b53860ab254b">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period accommodates delays in automatic deductions, supporting the effectiveness of the monthly payment schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="70feef39-e3b5-4a93-9e69-79a091efe2e9">
      <data key="d3">While the grace period allows temporary continuation of coverage post-due date, it has no bearing on when the overall 20-year term ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="68115e7f-f7b6-423f-93fb-d3d8750f2e29">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage after a missed premium deadline; however, it does not affect or reference the identity of the primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d" target="24f6a5ad-25db-42dc-939d-c4d5b2ed9a0f">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage even if premiums are late, which indirectly supports the continuity of benefits payable to Sarah Elizabeth Anderson.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
