    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">The grace period is explicitly stated as lasting 31 days after the premium due date, providing time for payment without losing coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that coverage continues past the due date, allowing time for late payments while maintaining eligibility for benefits. However, even with ongoing coverage, the insurer requires official proof of death to disburse the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows additional time to pay the overdue premium without losing coverage. If payment isn't made by its conclusion, the policy terminates.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary coverage extension after missed payments, but it has no connection to how policy anniversaries are determined annually from the original issue date.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">The grace period ensures ongoing coverage beyond the due date, allowing time for payment. This supports timely claims processing, enabling the death benefit to be issued as a lump sum when needed.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continuous coverage beyond the due date, potentially enabling the death benefit to be claimed even if the premium was late, so long as death occurs before policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows continued coverage even if the premium is not paid by the due date. This ensures uninterrupted protection during the specified window.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payments without losing coverage, but it does not affect the suicide exclusion clause, which operates regardless of timely premium payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period begins immediately after the monthly premium due date, ensuring continuous coverage if paid within that window.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The grace period detail provides context about payment flexibility but does not relate logically to the claim that no other exclusions exist, especially since the policy includes a suicide exclusion.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures ongoing coverage beyond the due date, preserving the policyholder's ability to maintain eligibility for future benefits, such as converting to permanent insurance without medical evidence.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.55</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary coverage beyond the due date, allowing time for payment; however, it has no impact on how future premiums are calculated if the policyholder chooses to convert later.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary leeway for premium payment, but it does not affect the deadline for converting the policy to permanent insurance, which depends solely on policy expiry or the insured reaching age 65.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary coverage beyond the due date, but it does not influence how premiums are calculated when converting to a permanent policy later.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
