      <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium within the 31-day grace period triggers the loss of coverage, making timely payment contingent on the length of this buffer period.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period leads to loss of coverage, underscoring the importance of timely payment during that window.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates that coverage ends if payment isn't made by the grace period’s end; this outcome corresponds exactly to the policy lapsing described in fact sentence 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The grace period allows delayed payments without immediate loss of coverage, making it possible for the policyholder to avoid lapsing despite missing the initial due date.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period ends coverage, meaning no death benefit can be claimed regardless of when death occurs relative to policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid within the grace period, coverage ends, meaning no death benefit can be claimed even if proof of death is submitted later.</data>
      <data key="d4">TERMINATES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, coverage terminates, meaning no death benefit would be available. Therefore, the lump-sum disbursement described in fact_sentence_2 cannot occur under such circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">If the premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it's no longer active. As a result, the insurer cannot pay the death benefit unless the policy was still in force at the time of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONS PAYMENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums are due monthly on the 15th establishes the schedule against which the 31-day grace period operates, defining when payment deadlines occur relative to the grace period's start.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
