    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is in force—including during the grace period—the death benefit becomes payable. Therefore, the existence of an active policy status, maintained through the grace period, supports the condition required for benefit disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is in force—including during the grace period—the death benefit is payable, making the grace period critical for maintaining eligibility under fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit hinges on the policy being in force at the time of death. Since the grace period preserves the policy's status during delays in premium payments, it enables the fulfillment of this financial commitment by preventing premature lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy is still in effect at the time of death. This requires that the premium has been paid within the grace period; otherwise, the policy would have lapsed, making the benefit non-payable.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the insured dies while the policy is in effect. This means that any lapse caused by missing payments beyond the grace period would prevent the payout, making timely premium payment critical.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable upon the insured's death while the policy is in force, regardless of whether it coincides with a policy anniversary.</data>
      <data key="d4">IRRELEVANT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable upon the insured's death while the policy is in force, but only if that death happens prior to the policy's expiry date. Without meeting this time constraint, even an otherwise eligible claim would not result in a payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only triggered if the policyholder's death occurs while the policy is active, but it cannot be paid out unless official proof of death is submitted by the beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRES_PROOF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is in force, the death benefit becomes payable. This benefit is typically issued as a lump sum unless otherwise selected by the beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">PAYMENT_METHOD</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable only if the insured dies while the policy is in force, which includes the grace period when premiums are overdue but coverage persists.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 does not apply if the insured dies by suicide within two years of the policy's issue date, as specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit provision ensures payment to beneficiaries upon the insured's death while the policy is active. This feature operates independently of the policyholder's ability to convert to permanent insurance later.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the core condition for death benefit payment. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that only known exclusions (like suicide) exist, reinforcing confidence in the claim eligibility defined by sentence 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The grace period ensures the policy stays active beyond the due date, preserving eligibility for the death benefit if the insured passes away during this time.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy remains in force, which depends on consistent premium payments made according to the specified schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit depends on the policy being active at the time of death, which may require actions like conversion by age 65 to maintain that status. Conversion availability ensures ongoing coverage options that support sustained eligibility for benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit upon the insured's death while the policy is in force does not depend on the method used to calculate premiums after conversion. This fact focuses on claim conditions, whereas the second concerns future pricing under a different policy type.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit upon the insured's death while the policy is in force is independent of the premium calculation method used when converting to permanent insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence describes the condition under which the death benefit is paid—when the insured dies while the policy is active. The second sentence explains how premiums are determined for a future conversion to permanent insurance, unrelated to immediate death benefit disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit provision depends on policy status at time of death, while the conversion option is influenced by the insured’s age when exercising it. These elements operate independently within different stages of the policy lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 may depend on whether the policyholder converts coverage, as the resulting policy's terms—and thus its payout potential—are influenced by the amount of coverage selected at conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 depends on the policy remaining in force, which is influenced by the successful conversion to a permanent policy; thus, the class of permanent policy selected determines whether continued coverage—and hence future death benefit eligibility—is maintained.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 depends on the existence of an active policy; the grace period described in fact_sentence_1 preserves policy status, enabling eligibility for the death benefit when the insured passes away.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the trigger for paying the death benefit; fact_sentence_1 clarifies what the death benefit actually is, providing necessary meaning to the event described in sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit hinges on the policy being active, which depends on premiums being paid by the due date—specifically the 15th of the month—as defined here.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="939a63b2-7c6f-4272-b3bb-df11d504c2e5" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">eligible_for_payment_when_insured_dies_while_policy_in_force</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5d4d9431-5ac5-4d0e-b78f-15656e4c1935" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines policy in-force status</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="3b7c6bdd-84a5-45e1-a161-9d482a80a078">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="19dd2d31-2bd6-42fd-8cda-131b7dac01d0">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="b000929b-7616-4055-b14f-a26612fe0abd">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">POLICY_TERM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="0d07db10-fb03-4b5e-848a-1edfb2174aca">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="ffbab753-f8b7-45d3-9b7f-f80fd99a6ce7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="86780fb2-181c-423c-87b2-34846da85a39">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="828442ef-217f-4100-9e95-88952e4870f7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="89e83c51-a7a3-4eff-848a-de2b8d2025c2">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">To receive the death benefit, proof of death must be submitted. This requirement stands independently of whether the policyholder used the 31-day grace period to maintain coverage through a missed payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">Even though coverage may continue past the due date via the grace period, the death benefit cannot be issued without proper proof of death being verified.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">Receiving proof of death is required to initiate the death benefit process, which assumes the policy remained in force—such as through timely payment or use of the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">To receive the death benefit, proof of death must be provided. However, if the policy has already lapsed due to missed payments beyond the grace period, such proof becomes irrelevant because the policyholder would no longer have an active policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary to receive the death benefit; however, such a claim cannot succeed if coverage was already terminated due to missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 requires submission of proof of death to receive the death benefit, a condition independent of any policy anniversary. Fact sentence 1 explains what constitutes a policy anniversary but does not influence or relate to the claims process described in sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">Receipt of proof of death is mandatory for processing the death benefit; without such documentation, even an active policy does not result in a payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES_PAYMENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 requires proof of death to initiate benefit payment; however, such proof is only relevant if the death occurred before the policy expired, making it contingent on the timing specified in fact sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted to initiate the claims process; only after verification is the death benefit distributed, typically as a lump sum unless otherwise selected by the beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The need to submit proof of death is unrelated to the availability of a 31-day grace period for late premium payments. One pertains to claim validation, the other to policy maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The need to submit proof of death does not affect or relate to when premiums are due each month; they pertain to separate stages of the policy lifecycle—one concerning claims initiation, the other financial obligation fulfillment.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of death depends on continued coverage; if coverage lapses, no claim can be made. The grace period ensures continuity, enabling the process outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for proof of death is subject to a restriction if suicide occurs within two years of issuance, in which case the insurer's obligation is reduced to returning premiums rather than paying the full death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The need for proof of death to trigger the death benefit is confirmed as the sole procedural requirement, since no other policy exclusions limit eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide proof of death is necessary to trigger the payment of benefits but does not influence or depend on the ability to convert the policy into permanent insurance later.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit claims require official proof of death, but this condition does not influence how premiums are calculated for future policy conversions.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide proof of death ensures that beneficiaries can access the death benefit when eligible. This step is independent of the timeline for converting the policy into permanent insurance, which has its own cutoff conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the condition required to receive a death benefit, specifically the need for documented proof of death. This does not influence or relate to how premiums are calculated during a policy conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit claims require official proof of death, but this condition does not influence how premiums are calculated upon policy conversion. The timing and documentation of death do not affect the actuarial basis used for converted policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for proof of death does not influence the insured's age-based conversion outcome; these are separate procedural and eligibility criteria within the policy framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the requirement for proof of death to trigger a death benefit, whereas fact_sentence_2 explains that the level of coverage selected during conversion impacts the resulting policy terms. These statements address different procedural phases: claims processing versus conversion decisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for claiming benefits, regardless of the permanent policy class selected during conversion; however, the choice of policy class impacts whether conversion is viable at all.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is required to claim the death benefit; the grace period allows the policyholder's estate sufficient time post-due date to provide such documentation without losing coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death, mentioned in fact_sentence_2, is necessary to trigger the death benefit outlined in fact_sentence_1, making it an essential prerequisite for claim settlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for claiming the death benefit, but such a claim can only succeed if the policy was not lapsed—meaning premiums were paid on time, particularly by the 15th of each month as specified.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0d07db10-fb03-4b5e-848a-1edfb2174aca" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">requires_proof_of_death</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="1424b3b6-97b8-4080-9394-5e538136c075">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="63939041-c06d-497a-bba4-b98cd32b97a8">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="4bec5cd7-f865-48be-8c29-2c506c4be29c">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">POLICY_TERM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="e19c3be6-6d91-4167-8ab6-c69c0d2049d1">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="2f80ac7e-9044-420f-8dba-94a65359bfc7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="528615b5-a762-4798-ade1-23d5f7913ede">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="3a909d39-dd4d-4857-bfeb-ab6dae321851">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="8a09d9e2-7f16-4adc-b701-cb75bef407c7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be paid, the insured must die before the policy expires, meaning timely premium payments—including those made during the grace period—are necessary to maintain coverage until that point.</data>
      <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable, the insured must die before policy expiry; this requirement relies on continued coverage, maintained through the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to apply, the death must occur prior to policy expiry; thus, the existence of a grace period increases the window during which such deaths could qualify, reinforcing its importance.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable, the policy must remain in effect until death; therefore, timely premium payment—even within the grace period—is necessary to maintain eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.87</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be payable, the policy must still be active; thus, timely premium payments ensuring continued coverage are required prior to death.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">Death benefits are contingent on the insured dying prior to policy expiry, meaning the policy’s end date—a fixed point determined at inception—is critical. The 'Policy Anniversary' serves as an annual reference point used to monitor how close the policy is to expiring.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be paid under the policy, the insured must die before the policy ends; however, this depends on the policy being actively in force at the time of death, ensuring continuous coverage up to that point.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">For the death benefit to be paid under any circumstances, the insured must die before the policy expires; even with proper proof of death, payment is denied if the death occurs post-expiry, rendering the requirement in fact sentence 1 irrelevant otherwise.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence defines when the death benefit becomes payable—only before policy expiry. The second explains that, once payable, it is distributed as a lump sum by default, regardless of the timing condition.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONS PAYMENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage even after missing a premium, allowing the death benefit to remain applicable if death occurs during this extended timeframe prior to policy expiry.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">If the insured dies before policy expiry, the death benefit generally applies; however, if the death is by suicide within two years, the benefit is restricted to a refund of premiums instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies when the death benefit is payable, while fact_sentence_2 confirms that no additional restrictions exist beyond what's already outlined, supporting the validity of the condition set forth in sentence one.</data>
      <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit eligibility depends on timing relative to policy expiry, but this does not influence how premiums are calculated when converting to permanent insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry ensures claim validity, while the 31-day grace period helps maintain active coverage despite missed payments, thereby preserving eligibility for the death benefit under the stated conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORTS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death benefits be paid only before policy expiry ensures timely claims processing, while the recalculation of premiums based on attained age at conversion affects long-term affordability. These clauses operate independently but contribute to policy integrity.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit eligibility depends on timing relative to policy expiry, unrelated to the calculation method used for converted policy premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that the death benefit depends on the insured dying before the policy expires. This condition aligns with the timeframe mentioned in fact_sentence_2, which limits when conversion to permanent insurance may occur, emphasizing the importance of the policy expiry date as a critical boundary.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit eligibility depends on the insured dying prior to policy termination, while the conversion right allows transitioning to permanent insurance without health verification, potentially extending coverage beyond original term limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">Death benefit eligibility depends on the timing of death relative to policy expiry, independent of when premiums are paid. Monthly premium deadlines do not affect whether the death benefit is triggered by an early death.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The conditionality of the death benefit depends on timely policy maintenance; however, the ability to convert to permanent insurance—affected by attained age—provides a pathway that could extend coverage beyond initial term limits, thereby potentially enabling future claim eligibility depending on when conversion occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The condition for receiving a death benefit prior to policy expiry does not affect the outcome of converting coverage to permanent insurance, though both involve policy duration constraints. Conversion success depends on the selected coverage level regardless of when death might occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry may be affected by the permanent policy class chosen during conversion, as different classes have varying terms and durations influencing when benefits become available.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry makes the grace period relevant, as it helps maintain active status long enough for claims to qualify when death happens near the deadline.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the temporal condition for payout; fact_sentence_1 explains the financial consequence of meeting that condition—the disbursement of the specified benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry depends on sustained premium payments; missing the 15th due date could trigger lapse unless covered by the grace period, thus linking the due date to benefit eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e19c3be6-6d91-4167-8ab6-c69c0d2049d1" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">payout_conditioned_on_death_before_policy_expiry</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3a909d39-dd4d-4857-bfeb-ab6dae321851" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">temporal condition for death benefit payout</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="7f2c82b5-b6a5-424b-900a-95d4286770ac">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="50aa11bf-917a-4384-bf22-3c36197c9711">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="b0229b3d-5c61-4a82-958c-9121e941ba22">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">POLICY_TERM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="dd1b45c4-a597-47b9-93d6-2ff6581aa181">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="e4e18c05-584e-42d9-9fab-a524030fac69">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="1c25be3a-5f3c-4b0f-b9f4-dce24c360f97">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="18a354de-5c3e-4bf4-8a0f-ca8af9391ad4">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="fea4f30e-c7e4-4901-bd19-1e4e67e5d56d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">DATE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="00310326-ecb4-4736-a477-d83d6eec65e1">
      <data key="d3">The standard payout of the death benefit as a lump sum reflects typical settlement practice, which operates independently of whether the premium was paid within the grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="be5e26fa-04fc-4729-9543-1bbeb100990a">
      <data key="d3">The standard lump-sum payout of the death benefit assumes the policyholder was covered at time of death, which depends on timely payments or being within the grace period, as noted in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="ea388ad9-aea7-4e92-83b0-81362c2d48be">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is generally paid as a lump sum, regardless of whether the premium was paid on time or during the grace period. The timing of payment does not alter the disbursement method.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Even if the policy lapses due to non-payment, the manner in which the death benefit would be paid—if applicable—is still determined by the settlement options available at time of claim, regardless of lapse status.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit being paid as a lump sum assumes the policy was active at the time of death; however, if coverage terminated due to non-payment beyond the grace period, this payout condition does not apply.</data>
      <data key="d4">PREVENTS_PAYOUT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable when the insured dies while the policy is active, and it is generally distributed as a lump sum unless the beneficiary opts for another method.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid as a lump sum if the beneficiary opts for that settlement; however, this distribution requires prior submission and acceptance of proof of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies the standard payment format—the lump sum—for the death benefit. This detail holds true irrespective of whether the death occurred before policy expiry, as defined in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">PAYMENT FORM</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">The statement about lump-sum death benefit payments does not depend on or reference the concept of a 'Policy Anniversary,' which marks yearly anniversaries of issuance rather than payout conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit's lump-sum payment option is unrelated to the schedule of monthly premium due dates. This statement describes how proceeds are distributed but does not reference or rely on when premiums are paid.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid as a lump sum by default, but this does not influence or relate to the ability to convert the policy into permanent insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is generally paid as a lump sum, but if suicide occurs within two years of issuance, the insurer's obligation is restricted to returning only the premiums paid, effectively nullifying the full lump-sum payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit's lump-sum payment option is unrelated to the availability of a 31-day grace period for late premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit payout options are independent of when a policyholder may convert to permanent insurance. This statement describes how proceeds are distributed but does not relate to conversion timelines.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is paid as a lump sum by default, but beneficiaries may choose alternative options. This detail does not influence or relate to how premiums are calculated upon policy conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the standard payout form of the death benefit as a lump sum. This detail is unrelated to whether other exclusions exist beyond the known ones.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The manner in which the death benefit is disbursed does not affect whether coverage persists during the grace period. The timing and conditions of payout are independent of continuation of coverage post-due date.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit's lump-sum payment option does not influence or relate to how premiums are calculated for a converted permanent policy.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit's lump-sum payment option does not influence or relate to how premiums are calculated upon policy conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit payment method described in fact_sentence_1 may indirectly depend on prior decisions such as conversion, where the insured’s attained age plays a role in determining final policy terms and costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The choice of conversion amount affects long-term benefit outcomes, indirectly influencing whether beneficiaries receive payments via lump sum or alternative options later. However, it does not alter the immediate lump-sum default rule stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The default lump-sum payment of death benefits depends on the beneficiary's choices, but the available settlement options may vary depending on the permanent policy class selected during conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a lump-sum death benefit depends on the policy remaining active; the 31-day grace period preserves this activity, ensuring payouts remain possible despite delayed payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_COVERAGE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the typical payment form of the death benefit—a lump sum—which directly supports and contextualizes the nature of the $500,000 benefit described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a lump-sum death benefit depends on maintaining continuous coverage through timely premium payments, such as those required on the 15th of each month as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
