    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="637866d8-58b3-46e9-bfc7-f6fae898630c">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for a converted policy depend on the coverage amount chosen, regardless of whether the original policy lapsed due to non-payment. The lapse condition is independent of the pricing mechanism used post-conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="74f91656-5a40-43ff-9624-5be0747c6603">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for converting to permanent insurance depend on the chosen coverage amount. This option is only available before the policy lapses, meaning it assumes the grace period was respected.</data>
      <data key="d4">PREVENTS_LAPSE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="15f70e44-bcd8-4fe7-aa61-1b7eaf9f1349">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for a converted policy are determined by the level of coverage selected; this determination is independent of the policy anniversary date.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The premium for a converted policy being determined by the amount of coverage selected has no direct bearing on whether the death benefit is paid upon the insured's passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that the premium for a converted policy depends on the selected coverage amount. This information is unrelated to the documentation needed to claim a death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for a converted policy are calculated based on coverage level, independent of whether the original death benefit was payable.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">Premium calculation based on converted coverage amount has no bearing on whether the death benefit is paid as a lump sum or through another option.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder converts to permanent insurance, the resulting premium is recalculated based on the desired coverage amount. This adjustment occurs regardless of the original monthly due date, though it operates within the framework established by regular premium obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Premium adjustments during policy conversion are determined solely by the chosen coverage amount and current age—not influenced by whether a grace period was used previously.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for a converted policy depend on the selected coverage level, independent of whether the original policy was paid within a grace period.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The second sentence specifies that the premium for a converted policy depends on the chosen coverage amount. This information does not relate to the suicide exclusion rule described in the first sentence, which governs payout eligibility rather than premium calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">The determination of the new policy’s premium based on coverage amount is independent of whether additional exclusions exist. This pricing rule holds regardless of the presence or absence of further exclusions.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The premium for the converted policy depends on the coverage amount chosen, which only becomes relevant if the option to convert without medical evidence is available.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The amount of coverage selected for conversion determines part of the premium, which is further adjusted according to the insured's attained age at the time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The premium for the converted policy is set according to the level of coverage chosen, independent of the conversion deadline. While the timing restriction governs whether conversion is possible, the actual cost calculation relies only on the selected benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT OF TIMING</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac">
      <data key="d3">The premium for the new policy depends on the extent of coverage being converted, and this amount interacts with the specific class of permanent policy selected, which further shapes the overall cost.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance depends on maintaining active status through timely payments or use of the grace period, so the existence of the 31-day grace period enables eligibility for conversion under favorable conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR_CONVERSION</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a defined death benefit enables the calculation of premiums under conversion options, making it foundational to determining costs in upgraded policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">The rule that converted policy premiums depend on coverage amount implies that any change in coverage could affect the monthly payment schedule, potentially influencing whether the 15th due date remains relevant under revised terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
