      <data key="d3">The determination of premiums for a new permanent policy based on its classification has no bearing on whether the death benefit is paid as a lump sum.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="964764d9-dfdd-4820-9bcd-3378418cf555">
      <data key="d3">When converting to permanent insurance, the premium amount adjusts based on the chosen policy class. This adjustment assumes ongoing adherence to the original monthly payment schedule outlined in the initial agreement.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for the converted permanent policy are determined by its classification, independent of whether a grace period was used when paying the original premium.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_DIRECT_RELATION</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">Premiums for a newly converted permanent policy depend on the chosen policy class, while the grace period allows temporary coverage extension if a premium is delayed—these concepts operate independently in the policy lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="a00a97b2-e4e5-454c-aabc-bb7861c62db6">
      <data key="d3">The second sentence describes how conversion to permanent insurance triggers recalculation of premiums based on the chosen policy class. This process is unrelated to the suicide exclusion rule described in the first sentence, which governs claim eligibility under specific circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="717aac5d-150f-48ca-8d8c-4a8f6ad91954">
      <data key="d3">The premium amount for the converted permanent policy is calculated according to its classification, which relies on the prior allowance of conversion without medical underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="883362bb-b7cf-40c8-9801-eb185d0f0958">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that the premium amount for a converted permanent policy depends on the policy's classification. This detail is independent of whether other exclusions exist, as it pertains solely to cost determination.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="c42788ae-930f-4f31-8775-d205d38dc828">
      <data key="d3">The determination of the new premium based on the policy class assumes that conversion has occurred within the allowed timeframe specified in the prior clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="65760e57-7d92-40e5-bf11-d6031579bc4b">
      <data key="d3">The choice of permanent policy class sets the baseline premium tier, which is further adjusted according to the insured's attained age at time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="91b85462-1151-4d24-8a71-6adf0d18e83a">
      <data key="d3">The choice of permanent policy class directly affects the premium rate, which is adjusted according to the amount of coverage being converted into the new policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">While the grace period allows temporary extension of coverage, the eventual cost of switching to a permanent policy hinges on its classification, making long-term financial planning dependent on timely decisions made during the grace window.</data>
      <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="178f1ff5-b810-4b49-ac2e-26311d446d64">
      <data key="d3">While the death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 pertains specifically to a term policy, its existence informs why one might consider switching to a permanent policy—a move whose associated premiums are determined by the class of permanent policy, as noted in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86082134-46ed-4548-a27f-2a5fed9c25ac" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">While the first fact sets a clear monthly due date ($45 paid on the 15th), the second fact suggests that converting to a permanent policy may result in different premium calculations, potentially changing when and how much is owed, thus affecting the applicability of the original due date rule.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
