    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s attained age influences how favorable the conversion terms may be, while the selected coverage amount determines the extent of protection post-conversion. Together, they shape the overall feasibility and cost of the new policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd">
      <data key="d3">Conversion eligibility based on attained age applies prior to the insured’s passing and does not influence the required documentation for filing a death claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns criteria for converting a term policy into a permanent one based on age, while the second specifies the mailing destination for claims. There is no direct connection between the process of conversion and the location for submitting claims.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="93c2148f-1bce-4ce3-bc8c-ba54d157bd99">
      <data key="d3">The insured's attained age influences whether they qualify for converting their policy, but this does not affect where claims must be filed after death.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="4f67aca9-2ed1-4582-9192-9aa38dccf3e4">
      <data key="d3">Conversion eligibility depends on the insured’s attained age, but this does not influence the requirement to submit the original policy for a death benefit claim.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">An individual’s attained age influences the available options and premiums during conversion, which may limit or expand access to certain permanent policy classes. Conversely, selecting a specific policy class sets expectations for coverage and pricing that depend on the insured’s current age.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="48cefe40-498d-4ea8-8c59-1a68bc65d395">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s attained age determines eligibility for converting the policy, but this factor does not influence whether the insurer can later contest the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="1f53ae68-2eb4-4755-b66c-aa693a6029cb">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence addresses how the insured's age impacts conversion options, while the second gives the physical location for sending claims documents. There is no direct connection between age-based conversion criteria and where claims should be mailed.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="6946e734-a717-40f6-a7c6-8217055992b2">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns conversion eligibility tied to the insured's current age, whereas the second focuses on correcting benefits when gender was inaccurately reported during application. They address separate procedural conditions without direct interaction.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc">
      <data key="d3">Attained age impacts whether conversion is allowed or favorable, but it does not influence how the company adjusts benefits due to misstated sex. This fact stands independently from considerations about gender-based premium recalculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="1dc42f01-adb8-4c75-b203-736d121f74ba">
      <data key="d3">The conversion outcome depends on the insured’s attained age, which could vary over time relative to when the document was issued. However, the document’s issuance date alone does not influence that dependency.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the insured's current age impacts their ability to convert the policy, whereas the second describes the formal requirement for making a policy assignment legally enforceable against the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97">
      <data key="d3">The insured's attained age influences whether they qualify for conversion into a new policy type, but this does not affect their ability to assign the current policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s attained age determines eligibility and terms during conversion; if this age was incorrectly reported, the insurer adjusts the death benefit accordingly to match what could have been obtained at the true age.</data>
      <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="f60bbb6f-361a-478e-b45e-8d28c60a0370">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns eligibility criteria for converting a term policy into a permanent one based on age, while the second describes the insurer’s obligation to process claims promptly upon receiving complete documents. They address separate procedural phases within the policy lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="58227a0c-85bd-4ca0-9fe2-c849ab8cd359">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns age-based criteria affecting conversion rights under the policy. The second sentence clarifies that the insurer does not guarantee the legality or validity of assigned policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 discusses how the insured's current age influences eligibility for converting the policy, whereas fact_sentence_2 explains that the age recorded during a prior misstatement dictates the adjusted death benefit if inaccuracies were found. These concern separate procedural stages involving age but not directly dependent on each other.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="8d7ba03c-5d26-4e8f-82f7-df2f969ad60b">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns conditions under which an insured may convert their policy, specifically related to age. This does not influence or relate to the process of submitting a claim form after the insured’s death.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="89eb9f0b-fb9d-4ed0-96df-faae58d5ebda">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s attained age determines eligibility and terms when converting the policy, but this factor has no bearing on who signs the document. The signature authority is unrelated to personal demographic factors like age.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="cd33eeaf-204c-4c25-b6c4-d8f541f0238a">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s age at conversion impacts future policy terms, such as premiums and coverage, but does not affect whether the death benefit is paid if the insured dies while the policy is still in force.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="4e7f0ebe-b702-4139-8b00-7c2f414cdf49">
      <data key="d3">The insured's attained age at conversion has no bearing on the necessity or validity of providing proof of death for claiming benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="eb100753-e253-4af2-af0d-8207823389c7">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur before policy expiry determines payout eligibility, but the option to convert to permanent insurance based on attained age offers a mechanism to maintain coverage past the original term, thus preserving potential access to death benefits through extended protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="6a2ec98a-aa86-4cd5-8e76-1036cf6ac3da">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 focuses on how age at conversion shapes policy conversion outcomes, it does not alter the standard lump-sum payment rule for death benefits outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="929683b0-a1d7-47e6-974e-1af143ca05b4">
      <data key="d3">The impact of attained age on conversion determines whether the insured receives optimal terms; thus, preserving coverage during the grace period becomes crucial to avoid losing access to conversion options based on future aging effects.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43" target="6fa1329d-8d5f-4720-bf13-810d2404088a">
      <data key="d3">While the grace period ensures continued protection temporarily, it has no direct impact on the final conversion decision, which depends solely on the insured’s age at time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
