    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is part of the claims process that occurs after death and has no bearing on whether conversion was possible due to attained age.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is necessary to initiate a death benefit claim, regardless of prior decisions about converting coverage amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is necessary for initiating a death benefit claim, regardless of the previously selected policy class.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="8d7ba03c-5d26-4e8f-82f7-df2f969ad60b">
      <data key="d3">A certified copy of the death certificate supports the validity of the claim and is typically submitted alongside the claim form, ensuring compliance with procedural standards after initial submission.</data>
      <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide a certified death certificate precedes submission to the designated Claims Department, forming a key step in initiating the claims process.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="93c2148f-1bce-4ce3-bc8c-ba54d157bd99">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide a certified death certificate is a key step in initiating a claim, which must ultimately be delivered to SecureLife Insurance Company for processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="4f67aca9-2ed1-4582-9192-9aa38dccf3e4">
      <data key="d3">The submission of a certified death certificate supports the verification of the insured's passing, which is necessary before any other documents—like the original policy—are processed. This step enables the insurer to begin evaluating the claim formally.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="1f53ae68-2eb4-4755-b66c-aa693a6029cb">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide a certified death certificate precedes the act of sending the claim, forming part of the preparatory step before mailing. This ensures that only complete submissions are dispatched.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">The submission of a certified death certificate initiates the claims process, upon which the insurer evaluates whether adjustments to the death benefit are necessary due to misstated age.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a certified death certificate is part of the claims submission process, but it does not affect or rely upon whether a policy assignment has been acknowledged by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide a certified death certificate enables the insurer to verify the event triggering the claim, which may lead to subsequent review of demographic information such as sex, potentially affecting the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="f60bbb6f-361a-478e-b45e-8d28c60a0370">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is a key component of the complete documentation needed to trigger the insurer’s 30-day payment obligation.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97">
      <data key="d3">The need to provide a certified death certificate is essential for initiating a death benefit claim, independent of whether the policy has been assigned. This step ensures verification of the insured's passing before any payout occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is required to initiate a claim, but it does not influence how the benefit is recalculated due to prior misstatements in age.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="89eb9f0b-fb9d-4ed0-96df-faae58d5ebda">
      <data key="d3">The need to provide a certified death certificate is a prerequisite step in filing a death benefit claim. This requirement may necessitate official validation, potentially involving authorization from a senior company officer like the Chief Underwriting Officer.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="6946e734-a717-40f6-a7c6-8217055992b2">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is required to initiate a claim, though the actual payout may later be adjusted depending on whether the insured's reported sex at application was incorrect.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="58227a0c-85bd-4ca0-9fe2-c849ab8cd359">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a certified death certificate is part of the claims process but does not relate to the validity of policy assignments handled by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="48cefe40-498d-4ea8-8c59-1a68bc65d395">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is required to initiate a death benefit claim, but the insurer’s inability to contest the policy after two years ensures such a claim remains valid regardless of prior misstatements.</data>
      <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="1dc42f01-adb8-4c75-b203-736d121f74ba">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a certified death certificate is part of the claims process but is independent of when the policy document was issued.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="b9bffd3e-9339-46c9-88e5-c86723b048a8">
      <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is required to trigger payout, but only applies if the insured dies while the 20-year term remains active.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="b178757c-5941-42c0-9651-c1536385e35b">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a certified death certificate for claims depends on the policy being actively in force since its issue date of January 15, 2024, making the start date essential for validating the claim’s legitimacy.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="70feef39-e3b5-4a93-9e69-79a091efe2e9">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is required to initiate a claim, but such a claim is only valid if it falls within the policy’s term, specifically before January 15, 2044.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="6bf61b64-8ea1-4157-b63e-7ea1c96a8aa9">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate enables the beneficiary to receive the $500,000 death benefit outlined in the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">ENABLES_RECIPIENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="65530dff-13a5-4bc9-975b-c4c8ec2db1db">
      <data key="d3">While the death benefit claim requires a certified death certificate, consistent adherence to the premium due date maintains policy validity, enabling such a claim to be processed.</data>
      <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd" target="101a86f6-cba5-43af-ae57-a5d5f17d8c1d">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is essential for initiating the death benefit claim; however, the existence of a 31-day grace period allows additional time before coverage lapses, ensuring timely submission remains feasible even if premiums are delayed.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR_COVERAGE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
