      <data key="d3">The second sentence directs claims submissions to the Claims Department, whereas the first focuses on factors influencing successful conversion under the policy. There is no direct influence or sequence linking them.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">Submitting claims to the Claims Department of SecureLife Insurance Company is a required administrative step that operates independently of the specific permanent policy class chosen for conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="8d7ba03c-5d26-4e8f-82f7-df2f969ad60b">
      <data key="d3">The Claims Department at SecureLife Insurance Company receives submissions related to death benefit claims, including the completed claim forms required by beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">RECEIVES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd">
      <data key="d3">Submitting the claim to the Claims Department follows the preparation of essential documentation, including the certified death certificate, ensuring proper handling of the claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="4f67aca9-2ed1-4582-9192-9aa38dccf3e4">
      <data key="d3">Sending the claim to the Claims Department ensures that documents like the original policy are received and processed correctly during the claims submission process.</data>
      <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="93c2148f-1bce-4ce3-bc8c-ba54d157bd99">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the exact department—the Claims Department—for claim submission. Fact_sentence_1 offers a broader directive but aligns with the detailed location specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">SPECIFIES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="f60bbb6f-361a-478e-b45e-8d28c60a0370">
      <data key="d3">Submitting claims to the Claims Department initiates the process that triggers the insurer’s obligation to pay within 30 days of receiving complete documentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="1f53ae68-2eb4-4755-b66c-aa693a6029cb">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence instructs claimants to submit claims to the Claims Department at SecureLife Insurance Company. This direction is made precise by the second sentence, which gives the complete postal address—P.O. Box 5000, Hartford, CT 06102—for that department.</data>
      <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies the destination for submitting claims, ensuring proper routing. The second describes a potential outcome during claims processing when inaccuracies in age were disclosed, affecting benefit calculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to send claims to the Claims Department does not influence or relate to the policyholder’s ability to assign the policy. They pertain to separate administrative processes.</data>
      <data key="d4" />
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="48cefe40-498d-4ea8-8c59-1a68bc65d395">
      <data key="d3">Sending claims to the Claims Department ensures timely processing, though the company’s inability to contest the policy after two years protects the claimant regardless of when the claim is filed.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc">
      <data key="d3">The location for submitting claims is specified, but this does not influence or relate to how benefits are recalculated if the insured's sex was incorrectly reported.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19">
      <data key="d3">Claim submissions must be directed to the Claims Department, but the method of processing does not affect how the death benefit is recalculated after a misstatement is discovered.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="58227a0c-85bd-4ca0-9fe2-c849ab8cd359">
      <data key="d3">The instruction to submit claims to the Claims Department does not relate to whether SecureLife is liable for assignment validity. This statement concerns claim processing logistics, independent of assignment responsibilities.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="6946e734-a717-40f6-a7c6-8217055992b2">
      <data key="d3">Claim submissions must be directed to the Claims Department, but the determination of the corrected death benefit depends solely on the insured’s sex at the time of misstatement, independent of submission location.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="1dc42f01-adb8-4c75-b203-736d121f74ba">
      <data key="d3">The claim submission instruction does not depend on or relate to the document’s issuance date. The date serves as metadata about when the document was created, independent of routing procedures.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to send claims to the Claims Department does not influence or depend on the conditions for assigning the policy. They pertain to separate administrative processes.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
