    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="f99df0d3-695f-4ae7-a1f8-eaf509b3c369">
      <data key="d3">The second sentence describes how the insured’s age during misstatement affects the recalculated death benefit. This determination operates separately from the coverage amount used in conversion processes described in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="6a8c51d1-93b9-4569-86fd-03b5a2ff4a43">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the impact of historical age misrepresentation on benefit recalculations, independent of whether conversion is possible. In contrast, fact_sentence_1 focuses solely on present-age criteria affecting conversion rights, without reference to past misstatements.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="cb928733-e199-4fdb-837b-0be5aae920be">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s age at the time of misstatement governs the calculation of the corrected death benefit under the misstatement clause, regardless of the chosen policy class used for conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="8d7ba03c-5d26-4e8f-82f7-df2f969ad60b">
      <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit resulting from age misstatement has no bearing on the necessity or content of the claim form required for processing; it only affects the final payout after submission.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="ecc65c44-a48a-4f2a-aa01-37fdd58978fd">
      <data key="d3">The correction of the death benefit based on misstated age occurs after the claim is filed, regardless of whether the death certificate has been submitted.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="4f67aca9-2ed1-4582-9192-9aa38dccf3e4">
      <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit is calculated based on the insured’s age at misstatement, which may affect whether the submitted original policy is sufficient or requires additional verification during processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.35</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="93c2148f-1bce-4ce3-bc8c-ba54d157bd99">
      <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit under the misstatement provision is determined by the insured’s age when the error occurred; however, regardless of that calculation, claims still need to be submitted to SecureLife Insurance Company.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="e102366f-ab52-4878-8cf7-8763f33b2392">
      <data key="d3">The correction of the death benefit based on the insured's age at misstatement occurs regardless of the location or manner of claim submission.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="1f53ae68-2eb4-4755-b66c-aa693a6029cb">
      <data key="d3">If the insured's age was incorrectly stated, the death benefit may be adjusted accordingly; this correction process does not affect where claims must be mailed.</data>
      <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="f60bbb6f-361a-478e-b45e-8d28c60a0370">
      <data key="d3">Benefit corrections based on misstated age occur regardless of when claims are paid; however, the correction process itself doesn't impact the 30-day payment window once documents are received.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="48cefe40-498d-4ea8-8c59-1a68bc65d395">
      <data key="d3">The misstatement provision adjusts the death benefit according to the insured’s true age at the time of application, which only becomes relevant once the incontestability period has passed and the policy is legally protected from challenge.</data>
      <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="52ad74d3-5275-4b1c-9bcf-18120fb60997">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s age at misstatement directly influences the calculation of the revised death benefit, making it foundational to the adjustment process described in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="ef3425a0-1e50-49ab-b5a8-ef77f6ab44bc">
      <data key="d3">The insured’s age at the time of misstatement directly influences the revised death benefit, especially when the misstated sex affects premium calculations and final payout amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="58227a0c-85bd-4ca0-9fe2-c849ab8cd359">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the death benefit is recalculated if the insured's age was incorrectly stated, while the second states that SecureLife Insurance Company does not verify the legal validity of assigned policies. There is no direct connection between adjusting benefits due to misstatements and assigning policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="9bd83bcc-7ea7-4a63-aaa4-02253aecdc97">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the death benefit is recalculated if the insured's age was incorrectly stated, while the second states that the policyholder has the right to assign the policy. There is no direct connection between adjusting benefits due to misstatements and assigning ownership.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="173ed3d5-0eb1-4ff3-a7bb-5ccb01ff26f9">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the death benefit is recalculated if the insured's age was incorrectly stated, relying on the actual age at misstatement. This does not influence or depend on the process required for transferring ownership via assignment.</data>
      <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="89eb9f0b-fb9d-4ed0-96df-faae58d5ebda">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the death benefit is adjusted if the insured misrepresented their age, depending on their actual age at the time of misstatement. This explanation does not depend on who signed the document but rather on internal policy rules regarding corrections.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="6946e734-a717-40f6-a7c6-8217055992b2">
      <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit depends on the insured's age when the misstatement occurred; similarly, it also depends on the insured's sex at that time. Both attributes independently shape how the benefit is adjusted.</data>
      <data key="d4">EQUALLY_RELEVANT</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7d8ac6d1-e47e-4ba7-b0a0-e181d124cf19" target="1dc42f01-adb8-4c75-b203-736d121f74ba">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the death benefit is adjusted if the insured's age was incorrectly stated during application, depending on the actual age at misstatement. This explanation stands independently from the second sentence, which only specifies the issue date of the policy document without affecting or being affected by the misstatement rule.</data>
      <data key="d4">NONE</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.0</data>
    </edge>
